
						To the Russian programmers
						Is devoted....


			Version 3.02				 06.06.98

      The wearing is made on a basis SDL 13/03/98 (US/Canada)
         containing support of protocols X2 and V90 (56K)

        Specially is adapted for operation on Russian lines
               Including modems INTERNATIONAL!

Is added: the additional registers of set-up BUSY, DIALTONE, RINGING, RING
          adjustment S39 (level of a transmitt signal) on ALL countries,
          register of fixing UTR are entered, the change of the code of
          country and all other parameters on ATCxx = is allowed, change of
          the serial number of the modem, on sound during retrains, adjustment
          of levels DTMF of a set, level of the fax, preservation S14, the
          truncated short commands of choice of the connection protocol are
          added, the indicator of speed of connection is introduced on HS Led.

 !!! Attention, after flood filling by this SDL, set command of the 
     AT&F1, AT+SF, AT&W    Differently work Dialtone, Busy will be not possible.

I. Loading SDL.

** ATTENTION !  ONLY FOR MODEMS With Clock Freq = 20.16Mhz on ATI7 **

   The loading of this SDL in modem do use Xmodem, if the previous SDL 
   supports it :)
       AT ~ X!
        <Or> if you use SDL without it of support (for example 1995) you 
       it is possible to load ROM variant of SDL, use the FreeLSD.exe utility,
       but to do it under multitask OS it is not recommended.
     For loading it is ROM variant,you be able to use a batch file "! Go.bat "
       if to correct in it number COM of port on used by you.
     The installation of the modem in Windows 95 is made through "mdmcrv90.inf"
      the file, according to the documentation from 3COM.

In detail about IDSDL:

   1. The change of the serial number of the modem (at any time, any number of
      times)  command of  AT~S-mmddyy-XXXXXXXXXXXX 
      where is : mm - month, dd - day, yy-year of this SDL, 
                 XXXXXXXXXXXX - serial number (any characters).

   2. It is authorized to use commands ATCxx=yy
    2.1 Example:  you possibly change the modem country:

        ATGN < - though it also is not necessary
        ATC10 = x, where x can have of significance:
         0 = USA/Canada	    10 = New Zealand
	 1 = Japan 	    11 = Czechoslovakia
	 2 = Finland	    12 = Belgium
	 3 = Sweden	    13 = Denmark
	 4 = UK		    14 = Australia
	 5 = Norway	    15 = France
	 6 = Switzerland    16 = Germany
	 7 = Netherlands    17 = International
	 8 = South Africa   18 = Austria
	 9 = Italy	    19 = Ireland 
	ATNX < - it is necessary

    2.2 Exampe:  inclusion of protocol X2 and V90

	ATGN
	ATC8 = 31
	ATNX (modem nothing will answer)

	AT&F1
	AT&W
	ATZ

    3. The adjustment of a level of a signal by the register s39 for want
        of any codes of country (including US/Canada) is allowed.
        Register can accept significance: 1 max. - 29 min!!!

    4. Setup of additional parameters by the AT command + S
	AT+SAn  - assignment of significance to the boolean register
	AT+S?   - View of all additional registers and their significances.
	AT+S$   - View of the help on additional + S register and command.
	AT+SF   - Setup in additional registers of the defaults.
	AT+Sn=m - assignment to the register "n" of decimal significance "m".
        AT+Sn=? - View extended regisrer.


II. Detailed: (all significances in the decimal system of calculation)

	+S1 - installation of hold time in ms. Between adjacent digits for
               want of set of number, can accept significance from 0 up to 127.
		Default - 70.

	To type digit consisting from more than 10 impulses, it is necessary to
	 place time of a pause between digits same, as well as time between
	 impulses in one digit.
	Specifying in number "/" "," or other characters of a pause it is
         possible to type numbers from arbitrary number of digits with an
	 arbitrary amount of impulses in each digit.
        In this case ATDP99/12/999 command will result in a set of three digits
	 consisting from 18, the 3-rd and 27 impulses.

	+S2 - installation of duration break/make for want of set of digit.
	 The significance 0 - by default, same duration will be for want
         of significance hexdecimal 8Ch (this is 140 in decimal):
           where 8 - is a duration of impulse,
                 C - duration of a pause between impulses.
           It is possible to reduce at that and other but in reasonable limits.
           Translate the turned out significance in the decimal form and bring
            in this register.

	 +S3 Management of recognition Busy/Dialtone prior to the beginning a
             set of number.
		Appointment separate bit:
		    20- to make filtering after processing
		    10- to make filtering before processing
		     8 - To clear bits on a mask 8Fh in hexdecimal (standard )
		     4 - To clear bits on a mask 73h (in addition) 
                         junior 2 bits - code of the function:
			0 - Nothing to change
			1 - Bit noise - > bit tone, noise to erase
			2 - Bit noise + bit tone - > bit tone
			3 - To erase bit noise

	The filtering allows selected and erase only single impulses. I.e. if
         with DSP the sequence [02 01 02 02] will come, after filtering the
         sequence [02 02 02 02] will be received. However, codes
         [ 02 02 01 01 02 02] will be transformed in [02 02 02 01 01 02].

	+S4 Management of recognition Busy/Dialtone after a beginning of a
             set of number. 
            Appointment of bits is similar to the register +S3.

   5.1 Technique of tuning of parameters Dialtone/Busy/Ringing

       Establish the additional registers AT+S3=0, AT+S4=0
       Establish ATX7.
       Turn On a mode of issue of the additional debug information ATY4.
       Turn On sound of the modem and connect modem to a line.

   5.1.1. Tuning Dialtone

       After a set of the ATD command you will see on the screen a sequence of
        digits.
       Bit 0 (the code 1) displays availability any of noise on a line.
        Will be further named "Bit noice".  
       Bit 1 (the code 2) displays availability of a signal with frequency
        425 Гц, i.e. Signal Dialtone/Busy/Ringing.
        Will be further named "Bit tone ".

	- If at you telephone station is normal, you will see streaming 02.
	  In this case +S3 set in 0.

	- If you see zero, it means, that your modem cannot detect any signal
           on a line, is probably on yours telephone station parameters of
           signals very much differ from generally accepted standart on
           frequency or amplitude.
	  In that case it is possible to try to achieve "02" changing
           significance of the register.
	 AT+S15, it is possible to use a number 0,1,2,4,8,16,32,64,128
	 (For example at me on coordinate telephone station all is caught
          only for want of AT+S15=4)

	- If you see units, it means, that your modem detects Dialtone as
	   a stranger of noise.
	  Then it is necessary to place AT+S3 in 1 (for want of it bit
           "noise" the tone "will move in bit") or in 2 (for want of it bit
           "noise" will be added to bit "tone").

	- If you see "03", it means, that your modem except for Dialton'а
 	   finds out also noise (or the level of a signal in a line hardly
	   is overestimated) It is possible отсечь bit noise (to write down
	   the code 3 in  AT+S3 ).
          Here the brief table of possible variants: codes the Register "+S3"
		02 set 0
		00 adjust AT+S15
		01 set 1 or 2
		03 set 1 or 2 or 3

	If the codes periodically vary:
		02/03  set 2 or 3
		02/01  set   2
		03/01  set   1

	- If in a sequence of codes there are codes more than 3, it is possible
	   them mask with the help of bits 2 and (or) 3 in the register "+S3"
           (adding to for significance of a mask 4 or 8)

	The register AT+S4 is adjusted similarly.

	5.1.2.  Tuning Busy

	The principle is similar to tuning Dialtone.
	Before the beginning of tuning it is necessary to place the register
         AT+S4=0 to give the command of a set of own number (or other, certainly
         occupied number).
         In time to hooters there should be двойки, for want of to pause - zero.
	- If so it also is - all wonderfully.
	- If there is only 0 - that a problem,it is possible again to return to
	  adjustment + S15 and to try it to pick up (at the same time of it pay
          attention to normal work DIALTONE) If nothing is received, it is
	  necessary to select from two variants, that it is more important or
	  more preferable: DIALTONE or BUSY :(

	Possible variants:

	0/1 - Dialtone is detected as noise. In AT+S4 it is possible to put
		significances 1 or 2 
	0/3 - Diatlone is detected as tone with impurity of noise.
		In + S4 it is possible to put significances 1, 2 or 3.
	1/3 - On a line constantly there is a noise. In +S4 it is possible to
		put significance 3.
	2/3 - The modem determines noise, as Dialtone, and Dialtone as noise.
		In +S4 it is possible to put significance 1.
	1/2 - In pauses the modem detects noise. In +S4 it is possible to put
		significance 3, in some cases 1.

	The main purpose of all these customizations - to achieve, that for
	 want of Dialtone on the screen were removed двойки without impurity
	 of other digits,for want of Busy and Ringing alternating "02" and zero.

	If for want of Busy the alternating "00" and "02" are removed, and the
	 employment is not defined, it is necessary to adjust of duration with
	 the help of the registers AT+S5, +S6, +S7, +S8.
	For want of RINGING the registers +S9, +S10, +S11 similarly act.

	Pay attention, that +S3 influences definition of signals up to a set
	 of first digit, and +S4 - later.

	+S5 - Minimum time of one signal BUSY (in 1/20 ms.).
		Standard significance - 10.

	+S6 - Maximum time of one signal BUSY.
		Standard significance - 35.

	+S7 - Minimum time of a pause between signals BUSY.
		Standard significance - 4.

	+S8 - Maximum time of a pause between signals BUSY.
		Standard significance - 255.

	+S9 - Minimum time of one signal RINGING.
		Standard significance - 9.

	+S10 - Maximum time of one signal RINGING.
		Standard significance - 125.

	+S11 - Minimum time of a pause between signals RINGING.
		Standard significance - 75.

	+S12 - Maximum number of the messages RINGING from the modem, on which
	     expiration NO ANSWER. For want of 0 - the counter is switched off.

	+S13 - Level of a signal (sensitivity) for recognition DIALTONE
		Standard significance - 525 (w)

	+S15 - Modifier of recognition DIALTONE
		Standard significance - 0

	+S16 - Level of a signal for a leased line.
		 Standard significance - 16384 (w)

	+S18 - is reserved (is not used yet)

	+S20 - Target level of the fax (w)
		 Standard significance - 16384 (w)

	+S22 - Level (sensitivity) of detecting DTMF
                 Standard significance - 525 (w)

	+S24 - Level of a signal of a voice-frequency set DTMF,
		for the first frequency.
		 Standard significance - 13000 (w)

	+S26 - Level of a signal of a voice-frequency set DTMF,
		for the second frequency
		 Standard significance - 3080 (w)

	+S28 - UTR bugfix (w) the constant, 
		is used for fixing an error "Unable To Retrain" can be
		useful on bad lines.
		 Standard significance - 7000 (w) USR puts - 1400

	+S30 - Minimum time of one period of a bell RING
		 Standard significance - 24

	+S31 - Maximum time of one period of a bell RING
		 Standard significance - 180

	+S32 - RING/Pause ratio 
		 Standard significance - 1024 (w)

	+S34 - Speed which for want of will be lit the indicator HS on the
		 external modem beginning with speed 2400!
		00 - Is not used (works under the standard USR, Default)
		03 - 2400
		04 - 4800
		05 - 7200
		06 - 9600
		07 - 12000
		08 - 14400
		09 - 16800
		10 - 19200
		11 - 21600
		12 - 24000
		13 - 26400
		14 - 28800
		15 - 31200
		16 - 33600

* Note: 1.(W) - means the two-byte register, can accept (0-65535), all other
		registers byte (0-255)
	2. All of duration of signals, in terms of on 20 msec.

   6. Logical switches (n = 0 or n = 1)

    AT+SAn - Tutn ON / Turn OFF sound during switching the speeds and retrains
    during the connect.
	"n" can accept significances:
		0 - Disable sound during switching the speeds and retrains
		      during the connect.
		1 - Enable sound during switching the speeds and retrains
	  	      during the connect.

    AT+SBn - modificator of sound during retrains.
	"n" can accept significances:
		0 - Turn On sound only retrain.
		1 - Turn On of any changes (for example change of speed)

    AT+SCn - to "not put"/"to put" a handset for want of to diagnostics
	 NO DIAL TONE.
	"n" can accept significances:
		0 - Standard processing NO DIAL TONE (to put a handset)
		1 - The changed processing NO DIAL TONE (to not put a handset)

	Is applied on the loaded telephone stations. If for want of removal of a
	handset for a set of number the modem has not heard DIALTONE (as has
	coincided with a source bell), the modem will issue NO DIAL TONE,
	but will not hang up,if after that to give ATA it will try to
	place connection. In FIDO T-Mail it is made 'AnswerOn RING NO DIAL TONE'.

     AT+SDn - Modifier of recognition of long hooters
		0 - Standard mode
		1 - To recognize long hooters (more than 1.5 sec.) as BUSY

     AT + SMn - Speaker management of the modem in a mode OFF Line
                0 - Speaker to switch off
	        1 - Speaker to switch on
       * This team is not remembered, but allows to include Speaker of the modem
         And to listen to a telephone line, for example for presence of
         conversation on parallel to the telephone device.
       * This team does not make go off hook.            

     7. Command of choice of the protocol of connection. 	

	AT+SSA - Automatic choice of the protocol (everyone are allowed, Default)
	AT+SSF - V.FC the protocol
	AT+SSH - HST the protocol
	AT+SST - V.32Terbo
	* If the remote modem is not capable will incorporate on the
	  established protocol, the connection on V.22bis (2400bps) or break
	  of connection is possible.

      8. Brief statistics on connection: the ATI9 command.

      9. HELP: the ATI13 command.

     10. Support of editing commands of memory ATG, ATGLK2

     11. AT%T - Recognition DTMF of codes 
        If the team AT%T will be given, it will be executed by a standard image.
        (Recognition and seal half-scientific DTMF of codes).
        If the ambassador %T there will be additional symbols, is caused 
        Extended %T
    * Independent go off hook these teams do not make.

        11.1 Complete format of the extended team:

 /* Syntax of teams extended DTMF, according to the standard */
 /*                  Konstantin Norvatoff                    */
                          
        %T + [time] passwd? Cmd1:cmd2

        Time - Waiting Time DTMF of codes (in seconds).
               If for this time, with the help DTMF, from ph. of a line will be
               The correct password is received, the team cmd1 will be executed,
               Team cmd2 differently will be executed. 
               In a waiting time, any symbol, received yours,
	 Of the computer through a COM-port, will interrupt expectation with a
         conclusion Message ERROR.

        Passwd - sequence of codes of the password.
	 If the code incoincident with the password, check will be accepted
	 Will begin at first (without any notices) and will be
	 Before the expiration of a waiting time "time" will proceed.
                The number of mistakes is not limited.

        Cmd1, cmd2 - usual teams (without prefix AT). 
		 If this line consists only of decimal figures, 
                She(it) is interpeted as number of the message 
	 (for example, it is possible to force the modem to give out
          the message VOICE (12)).

         Symbols "?" And ":" -space key.
         Have of plus in a team specifies the sanction, of removed,
          To operate by a level of a signal of the transmitter through
          the register S39,
         In this case at reception DTMF of a code ''('.')
          The following two codes (we shall name them x and y) will be
          interpeted as Decimal number. The meaning(importance) x*10 + y 
          will be brought in the register S39.
         Limiting meanings(importance) 1... 29, in case of an output for limits it
          range the team will be ignored.
         Allows calling "to order" a demanded level of a target signal.


        Example:

        %T[10] - coincides with %T, but in 10 seconds the analysis DTMF will be
                 Is stopped and OK will be removed.

        %T5 - will be indefinite to be expected a code 5. At input of a code will be given
                Diagnostics OK.

        %T[10]5
               - Too, but the code 5 should be entered during 10 seconds.
                If for this time it will not be entered, diagnostics is 
		given out ERROR.

	 %T+[10]5
               - Is similar previous, but the management S39 is authorized

        %T5?I1 - At input of a code 5 the team i1 will be executed.

        %T[3]7?I2
               - If for 3 seconds the code 7 will be entered, will be executed
                The team i2, differently will be deduced(removed) the 
                message ERROR.

        %T[20]123?A:X1DP!32
               - If for 20 seconds the code 123 will be entered, the modem will
                 begin to execute a team ATA, differently it will execute flash
                 and will type code 32 pulses metod by a set.

        %T[14]123?A:12
               - If for 14 seconds the code 123 will be entered, the modem will
               begin to execute a team ATA, differently it will deduce the 
               message VOICE or number 12 (if the mode of the numerical answers
               on ATV0) is included.

      * The team does not make go off hook independently,
        In most cases sequence should be
               ATH1%T [...].
      * Upon termination of connection (at use of an opportunity of the order S39),
        The modem is necessary init, for example on ATZ, for reset
        The changed meaning of the register S39.

